[1] int (xi(1-xi)-2)                 = -11/6    (non-soft part of K_gg)
    int_delta^{1-delta} K_gg          = -2*log(delta) - 11/6
    int (xi(1-xi)-2) ln(xi(1-xi))     = 67/18
    int xi^2+(1-xi)^2                 = 2/3
    int (xi^2+(1-xi)^2) ln(xi(1-xi))  = -13/9
    int xi(1-xi)                      = 1/6
    double-plus integral of real P_gg/(2N_c) = -11/6
[2] gluon loop constant (non-soft part, units of norm): CDR -67/9, Dpol=2: -64/9, shift 1/3
    -> cross section (alpha_s N_c/2pi)(67/9-pi^2/3)LO becomes (alpha_s N_c/2pi)(67/9-1/3-pi^2/3)LO, i.e. K -> K - N_c/6
    quark loop (CDR = Dpol=2, no gluon polarisation in the loop): constant 20/9 (units n_f T_R/N_c) ; pole coeff -2*int = -4/3
      -> 67/9 - pi^2/3 -> 67/9 - pi^2/3 - (20/9) n_f T_R/N_c ;  11/3 -> 11/3 - (4/3) n_f T_R/N_c = beta_0/N_c
    N_2b UV, xi(1-xi) part x (2/eps): CDR 1/(3*epsilon)   (finite extra: 0)
    N_2b UV, xi(1-xi) part x (2/eps): Dpol=2 (epsilon + 2)/(6*epsilon)   (finite extra: 1/6)
    Row II.IV, Dpol=2 minus CDR: -C int dxi [2*N_c*xi*(1 - xi)] Pi(xi)
[3] 1/(a b) + 1/(b D) - 1/(a D) = 0
[4] single-eps sum = -ell/2  (independent of beta_0 and N_f)
    two-eps: UV ell/2  IR -ell
[5] d sigma/d ln mu_R^2 = beta_0**2*(L_F - L_R)*Dg(L_F)*al(L_R)**3/(8*pi**2)  ; d sigma/d ln mu_F^2 = beta_0**2*(-L_F + L_R)*Dg(L_F)*al(L_R)**3/(16*pi**2)  (O(alpha^3) only)
[6] momentum sum rule for the conversion: c_delta = N_c/6  ; (alpha_s/2pi) c_delta = N_c/(12*pi) * alpha_s  vs  alpha_DR/alpha_MS - 1 = alpha_s N_c/(12 pi)
